title open problem 1: edit versus split, and the merge that still refuses

# Section 15, open problem 1, in two folders.
#
# Both folders report kind "content", and it is worth reading the two
# messages side by side: they refuse for quite different reasons.
#
# split/ -- onto un-deduplicates a hard-linked pair; off-of edits the
#   file through one of its names.  The duplication guard (Rule 9.8)
#   stops it, and says so in as many words: the edit "would have to be
#   written into 2 separate output pools, which is a write its author
#   never made".  Off-of wrote one file once.  Honouring onto's split
#   would turn that single write into two, and the guard will not
#   invent the second one.
#
#   The alternative is to propagate the edit into every unedited
#   fragment.  That is exactly right if the split was a deliberate
#   un-deduplication ("stop sharing this, I am about to change one of
#   them") and exactly wrong if it was not, and nothing in three
#   snapshots says which it was.  That is the whole question: the
#   evidence is silent, so a policy has to speak.  It is one switch.
#
# merged/ -- the sibling case the section asks for.  Both sides
#   perform the IDENTICAL merge, and one of them also edits.  Not one
#   thing about the structure is opposed -- both sides agree logo.png
#   and icon.png are one file now -- and it still refuses, because
#   pass 3's rule 2 finds the material of the merged pair coming from
#   two different base pools and will not pick between them.  This is
#   the case that most looks as though it ought to decide, and the one
#   to hold up when arguing about the guard.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: split/
      # one file, two names.
      10-100: report.pdf = pdf-v1
      10-100: report-copy.pdf
    3-100: merged/
      20-100: logo.png = logo-v1
      21-100: icon.png = icon-v1

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: split/
      # the un-deduplication: report-copy.pdf gets a dnode of its own,
      # same bytes.
      10-100: report.pdf = pdf-v1
      210-200: report-copy.pdf = pdf-v1
    3-100: merged/
      # the merge, and nothing else.
      20-100: logo.png = logo-v1
      20-100: icon.png

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: split/
      # the edit, through the name the pair still shares.
      10-100: report.pdf = pdf-v2
      10-100: report-copy.pdf
    3-100: merged/
      # the same merge, arrived at independently, plus an edit.
      20-100: logo.png = logo-v2
      20-100: icon.png

# --- expected result, generated by gen-expected.js ---
expect conflict content
expect quarantined /merged/icon.png
expect quarantined /merged/logo.png
expect quarantined /split/report-copy.pdf
expect quarantined /split/report.pdf

tree expected
  1-1: /
    3-100: merged
      20-100: icon.png = logo-v1
      20-100: logo.png
    2-100: split
      210-200: report-copy.pdf = pdf-v1
      10-100: report.pdf = pdf-v1
